      "judgment_rationale": "Web owns the complete MCP server lifecycle plus tool, prompt, and log authority. McpAppsTabV2 directly binds MCP Apps list, search, delete, refresh, and open-in-Canvas interactions, while the Canvas resource and tool-call context remains incomplete and therefore Web stays partial without claiming unbound proxy APIs. Desktop now has a real production loader, App binding and native settings management surface for refresh/list and create in both modes. The management Snapshot observations do not carry the authority_revision required by Snapshot v4, so Cloud and Local both fail closed to capability_authority_revision_unavailable even though their reviewed view, list and create contracts remain recorded. Additional detail, sync, test, reconcile, discovery and tool-call endpoints are not counted as native surface actions until a production UI binds them."
