      "judgment_rationale": "AcpDashboard reads status and runner pools, renders the Agent and session summaries embedded in status, and exposes external-Agent create, update, delete and test controls. Separate runner-instance, Agent-list, session-list and session lifecycle service methods are not called by the production page and are excluded from its API authority. Desktop now has a real production loader, App binding, typed client, controller and native Cloud management page with the same reviewed member and administrator actions. Its active client snapshot omits the authorityRevision required by tenantRemainingCapabilityClient, so Snapshot v4 normalizes it to tenant_acp_authority_contract_invalid and promotes no action. External ACP authority remains intentionally cloud-only for Local Desktop."
